# Third-party notices

The Tarsier source code is Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE). Third-party components remain under their own licenses. This inventory covers the Python 3.11 and 3.14 installs, the 3.11 fresh install and the npm lock file, on Windows. It is attribution and a review aid, not a legal conclusion.

## What is bundled

The repository tracks source code, package manifests/lockfiles, synthetic fixtures and the font/CSS imports. The Python wheel bundles the built browser assets, including Inter and Newsreader font files and the MapLibre worker, plus this notice and its linked license texts. The repository does not track Python or npm site-packages/node_modules binaries. Users install Python dependencies with pip and frontend build dependencies with npm; their platform wheels and optional native libraries may contain further terms.

**What this package copies:** the built web interface contains code from npm packages, including the libraries inside MapLibre GL JS, under permissive licences (such as MIT, ISC and BSD), and the Inter and Newsreader fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1). Their licence texts are linked below and included in the package. No LGPL, GPL or MPL code is copied into the package.

**Installed separately by pip from their own publishers:** psycopg and psycopg-binary (LGPL-3.0), pymssql (LGPL-2.1) and certifi (MPL-2.0). Some binary wheels also contain native libraries under LGPL or other terms, for example GEOS. lightningcss and pathspec (MPL-2.0) are used only to build.

This inventory covers Windows only, as the README does: Linux and macOS are not yet qualified and may install other packages. It has not been reviewed by a lawyer. Kuzu 0.11.3 is archived and unsupported upstream; that is a maintenance risk independent of license.

